    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d369">

                <pb facs="0377" n="261" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg261"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.00/1653.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Sullivan to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Santo Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-12-17T11:00:00-04:40">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 17, 1914, 11 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Have urged upon Dominican Government all reforms suggested by you and the same
                    are now under consideration. Dominican Government shows timidity of local
                    criticism rather than [?] to grant reforms. I recommend patience and tact for a
                    few weeks when I believe all said reforms will be substantially accorded.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sullivan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
